{"name":"Blues","hex":"#296a9d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blues","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of several sports teams whose uniform is predominantly blue, such as:\n The chariot-racing faction of the Roman circus and Constantinopolitan hippodrome that wore blue.\n\n Carlton Football Club.\n New South Wales.\n Birmingham City FC.\n Everton FC.\n Chelsea FC.\n Manchester City FC.","The chariot-racing faction of the Roman circus and Constantinopolitan hippodrome that wore blue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blues"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blues","blocks":[{"text":"Blues is a music genre and musical form that originated among African Americans in the Deep South of the United States around the 1860s. Blues has incorporated spirituals, work songs, field hollers, shouts, chants, and rhymed simple narrative ballads from the African-American culture. The blues form is ubiquitous in jazz, rhythm and blues, and rock and roll, and is characterized by the call-and-response pattern, the blues scale, and specific chord progressions, of which the twelve-bar blues is the most common. Blue notes, usually thirds, fifths or sevenths flattened in pitch, are also an essential part of the sound. Blues shuffles or walking bass reinforce the trance-like rhythm and form a repetitive effect known as the groove."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blues"},{"title":"Blues (Super Rugby)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blues are a New Zealand professional rugby union team based in Auckland, who play in the Super Rugby competition. Like New Zealand's four other Super Rugby teams, the Blues were established by the NZRU in 1996. One of the most successful teams in Super Rugby history, the Blues won the competition in its first two seasons, 1996 and 1997, and again in 2003 and 2024. Additionally, the team were finalists in 1998 and 2022, and semi-finalists in 2007, 2011 and 2023. They won a Trans Tasman competition in 2021."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blues_(Super_Rugby)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/MaRainey.jpg/500px-MaRainey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/MaRainey.jpg/500px-MaRainey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American blues singer Ma Rainey (1886–1939), the \"Mother of the Blues\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaRainey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Blues_shuffle_in_E.png/500px-Blues_shuffle_in_E.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Blues_shuffle_in_E.png/500px-Blues_shuffle_in_E.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typical blues shuffle rhythm; playⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlues_shuffle_in_E.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Sahel-Sudan.png/500px-Sahel-Sudan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Sahel-Sudan.png/500px-Sahel-Sudan.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Sahel (brown) and the Sudan (green)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASahel-Sudan.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-John-avery-lomax1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Musicologist John Lomax (left) shaking hands with musician \"Uncle\" Rich Brown in Sumterville, Alabama ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn-avery-lomax1_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/W._C._Handy_-_The_%22St._Louis_Blues%22_-_First_page.jpg/500px-W._C._Handy_-_The_%22St._Louis_Blues%22_-_First_page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/W._C._Handy_-_The_%22St._Louis_Blues%22_-_First_page.jpg/500px-W._C._Handy_-_The_%22St._Louis_Blues%22_-_First_page.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sheet music from \"Saint Louis Blues\" (1914)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AW._C._Handy_-_The_%22St._Louis_Blues%22_-_First_page.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/500px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/1280px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/500px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bessie Smith, an early blues singer, known for her powerful voice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABessie_Smith_(1936)_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/JohnLeeHooker1997.jpg/500px-JohnLeeHooker1997.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/JohnLeeHooker1997.jpg/500px-JohnLeeHooker1997.jpg?ut